```
Reason:
The unconditional invocation of `watchdog_enable` and `watchdog_disable` during CPU hotplug events allows these functions to be called on CPUs that are not part of the `watchdog_allowed_mask`, leading to the watchdog being enabled or disabled incorrectly, which can make it unstoppable.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (cpumask_test_cpu(cpu, &watchdog_allowed_mask))
    watchdog_enable(cpu);
```
```c
if (cpumask_test_cpu(cpu, &watchdog_allowed_mask))
    watchdog_disable(cpu);
```
Reason:
By wrapping the calls to `watchdog_enable` and `watchdog_disable` in a conditional check that verifies if the CPU is part of the `watchdog_allowed_mask`, the patch ensures that these functions are only invoked for CPUs that are intended to be monitored, thus preventing the watchdog from becoming unstoppable.

